  "prefLabel": "Env-Wr 402.03 Statutory Requirements for Certain Dams",
  "priorExpiration": "2005-08-20",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wr 402.03 Statutory Requirements for Certain Dams.\n\n(a) Pursuant to RSA 482:7, a new dam on a great pond shall not be constructed without specific authorization from the legislature.\n\n(b) The department shall hold a public hearing pursuant to RSA 482:30 and RSA 482:31 upon receipt of an application for construction or reconstruction of dams falling within the scope of RSA 482:17, and conduct the hearing in accordance with the provisions of Env-C 200 relative to non-adjudicative proceedings.\n\n(c) Pursuant to RSA 482:9, V, no permit to construct or reconstruct a significant hazard or high hazard dam shall be issued unless the requirements of that section are met.\n\nSource. #1716, eff 2-20-81; ss by #2207, eff 12-13-82; ss by #2900, eff 11-7-84, EXPIRED 11-7-90\n\nNew. #5080, eff 2-22-91; ss by #6462-B, eff 2-21-97; ss by #8285, INTERIM, eff 2-21-05, EXPIRES: 8-20-05; ss by #8414, eff 8-20-05; ss by #10510, eff 1-22-14; ss by #13980, eff 5-24-24",
